  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "idmap_ad — Samba's idmap_ad Backend for Winbind",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The idmap_ad plugin provides a way for Winbind to read id mappings from an AD server that uses RFC2307/SFU schema extensions. This module implements only the \"idmap\" API, and is READONLY. Mappings must be provided in advance by the administrator by adding the uidNumber attributes for users and gidNumber attributes for groups in the AD. Winbind will only map users that have a uidNumber and whose primary group have a gidNumber attribute set. It is however recommended that all groups in use have gidNumber attributes assigned, otherwise they are not working.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Currently, the [[p0]][[p1]][[p2]] backend does not work as the default idmap backend, but one has to configure it separately for each domain for which one wants to use it, using disjoint ranges. One usually needs to configure a writeable default idmap range, using for example the [[p3]][[p4]][[p5]] or [[p6]][[p7]][[p8]] backend, in order to be able to map the BUILTIN sids and possibly other trusted domains. The writeable default config is also needed in order to be able to create group mappings. This catch-all default idmap configuration should have a range that is disjoint from any explicitly configured domain with idmap backend [[p9]][[p10]][[p11]]. See the example below.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "ad"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "tdb"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p6]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p7]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "ldap"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p8]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p9]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p10]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "ad"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p11]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "IDMAP OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "range = low - high",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Defines the available matching UID and GID range for which the backend is authoritative. Note that the range acts as a filter. If specified any UID or GID stored in AD that fall outside the range is ignored and the corresponding map is discarded. It is intended as a way to avoid accidental UID/GID overlaps between local and remotely defined IDs.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "schema_mode = <rfc2307 | sfu | sfu20>",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Defines the schema that idmap_ad should use when querying Active Directory regarding user and group information. This can be either the RFC2307 schema support included in Windows Server 2003 R2 and newer or the Service for Unix (SFU) schema for versions before Windows Server 2003 R2. For SFU 3.0 or 3.5 please choose \"sfu\", for SFU 2.0 please choose \"sfu20\". Please note that the behavior of primary group membership is controlled by the [[p0]]unix_primary_group[[p1]] option.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default: rfc2307",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "unix_primary_group = yes/no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Defines whether the user's primary group is fetched from the SFU attributes or the AD primary group. If set to [[p0]][[p1]][[p2]] the primary group membership is fetched from the LDAP attributes (gidNumber). If set to [[p3]][[p4]][[p5]] the primary group membership is calculated via the \"primaryGroupID\" LDAP attribute.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "yes"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "no"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default: no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "unix_nss_info = yes/no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If set to [[p0]][[p1]][[p2]] winbind will retrieve the login shell and home directory from the LDAP attributes. If set to [[p3]][[p4]][[p5]] or the AD LDAP entry lacks the SFU attributes the options [[p6]]template shell[[p7]] and [[p8]]template homedir[[p9]] are used.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "yes"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "no"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p6]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p7]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p8]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p9]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default: no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "all_groupmem = yes/no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If set to [[p0]][[p1]][[p2]] winbind will retrieve all group members for getgrnam(3), getgrgid(3) and getgrent(3) calls, including those with missing uidNumber.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "yes"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default: no",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "deny ous",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This parameter is a list of OUs from which objects will not be mapped via the ad idmap module. If [[p0]][[p1]][[p2]] is set but [[p3]][[p4]][[p5]] is not set, every object outside the OUs listed in [[p6]][[p7]][[p8]] is allowed.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "deny ous"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
